# Normalise line endings.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true produces CRLF in the
# working tree while Prettier defaults to endOfLine: "lf". The result is
# `npm run format:check` failing locally on files whose content is already
# correct, and passing in CI, where the Linux runner checks out LF. That is a
# confusing split between machines, and with the three of us on different
# setups it would keep coming back.
#
# eol=lf (not just text=auto) forces LF in the working tree too, so the repo,
# every developer machine and CI all agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files git must not touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
